    text: "Tang children who were taught to read began with the Thousand Character Classic and the Classic of Filial Piety, often in a village or temple school; Dunhuang has yielded schoolboy copies with the pupil's name, date and doodles. Sons of officials and some talented commoners went on to the state schools and the examinations, where the jinshi degree, testing poetry and policy essays, became the path to prestige. Most children learned their parents' work instead. Artisans' sons trained in the official workshops or in their fathers' shops, girls learned sewing, weaving and silkworm rearing at home, and farm children herded, weeded and gathered fuel as soon as they could walk far.",
    wiki: ["Thousand Character Classic", "Imperial examination", "Classic of Filial Piety"],
