    title: "Lu Ban, Cai Lun and the patron gods of the trades",
    text: "Every trade in late imperial China had its patron, and every guild hall its altar. Carpenters and builders honoured Lu Ban, the legendary craftsman of Lu, and read his manual of building rituals; papermakers honoured Cai Lun; silk workers the Silkworm Goddess, often identified with Leizu; wine makers Du Kang; actors the Tang emperor Xuanzong; and many merchants the warrior Guan Yu, a god of loyalty and wealth. On the patron's birthday the guild held a feast, staged an opera, and burned incense and paper, and members swore to keep its rules. At home, shopkeepers set out offerings to the God of Wealth on the second and sixteenth of each month.",
