    title: "The Lü family community compact",
    text: "In 1076, the Lü brothers of Lantian, near Chang'an, drew up the first known community compact, a voluntary agreement among neighbours to encourage one another in virtue, correct one another's faults, observe proper rites and help one another in trouble. Members met monthly for a meal, a register recorded good deeds and faults, and there were clear duties: to help with fire, flood, theft, illness, funerals and the care of orphans, and to lend to those in need. Zhu Xi later revised the compact, and it became a model for village organisation across China and, as the hyangyak, in Korea. In practice, neighbours in a Song town shared wells, lanes, festivals and gossip, and watched each other closely.",
